      "t": "Tesla reveals SpaceX-powered Roadster that flies and falls with style",
      "d": "The new car used thrusters to leap over a Cybercab, Cybertruck, Tesla Semi, Model Y, and Model 3 at a demo in Texas.",
      "u": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/15/tesla-reveals-spacex-powered-roadster-that-flies-and-falls-with-style/",
      "m": "10. 16. AM 01:17",
      "ts": 1792113463000,
      "fullText": "Tesla just revealed its redesigned second-generation Roadster with SpaceX thrusters, a vehicle CEO Elon Musk has called &#8220;the best of the last of the human-driven cars.&#8221; Musk showed off the car at an event outside Waco, Texas, with a demonstration that saw the car use a mixture of high-powered fans and thrusters to drive up an inverted ramp, spin around, and ease itself to a landing on the pavement below. The car also used the thrusters to lift itself over a Cybercab, Cybertruck, Tesla Semi, Model Y, and Model 3 while in motion. &#8220;This will be the actual car that&#8217;s on the roads,&#8221; Musk said of the car, which Tesla showed accelerating 0 to 60 miles per hour in one second. &#8220;It literally is just going to puff itself up, and uh, and be able to do this, these maneuvers whenever you&#8217;d like.&#8221; Musk said Tesla will finally build the long-delayed vehicle in 2028, but didn&#8217;t name a price. Tesla will offer it in three trims. The first is &#8220;Performance,&#8221; which Tesla describes as &#8220;road ready.&#8221; It seats two, has active aerodynamics, and features a &#8220;multi-mode suction system for next-level performance on and off the track.&#8221; The second trim is &#8220;Thrust,&#8221; which is &#8220;race ready&#8221; and seats two, and has rear-mounted cold-gas thrusters that enable sub-one-second 0-to-60 mph acceleration. The third is &#8220;Rocket,&#8221; which is &#8220;air ready&#8221; and seats one, and has 10 cold-gas thrusters positioned around the car. All three trims will have 300 miles of range and be capable of speeds exceeding 230 miles per hour. Tesla&#8217;s website showed Thursday the company is taking reservations for the car, charging $50,000 just to reserve the Performance, and $250,000 for Thrust. The Rocket trim is billed as &#8220;invite only.&#8221; Tesla Roadster-starman Image Credits: Tesla Engineering VP Lars Moravy said at the event that the Roadster uses 10 thrusters connected to 600 liters"
